Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "created_at": signup timestamp that lets us keep only users who registered between 2019‑01‑01 and 2022‑04‑30.  
• "age": age of each user – used to find the minimum and maximum age in the filtered population.  
• "gender": user‑identified gender – used to produce separate results for males and females.  
• "id": the user primary key – useful when we need to count how many users belong to a specific age group after the filters are applied.  

Main conditions that will be reused  
• Restrict the signup window  
  "created_at" >= 1546300800000000      -- 2019‑01‑01 00:00:00  
  AND "created_at" <= 1651363199000000  -- 2022‑04‑30 23:59:59  
• Work on each distinct "gender" value (typically ‘M’ and ‘F’).

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (simple → complex) that progressively build toward the final answer.  
All column‑names are double‑quoted and each statement is limited to 20 rows at most.

```sql
-- 1. Description: quick glance at 20 raw user records
SELECT *
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: list the distinct gender values that exist in the USERS table
SELECT DISTINCT "gender"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: show a sample of users who signed up inside the required time window
SELECT "id", "gender", "age", "created_at"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "created_at" >= 1546300800000000 
  AND "created_at" <= 1651363199000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: count filtered users by gender (time‐window applied)
SELECT "gender",
       COUNT(*) AS "user_cnt"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY "gender"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: minimum and maximum age per gender inside the signup window
SELECT "gender",
       MIN("age") AS "min_age",
       MAX("age") AS "max_age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY "gender"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: list the users who meet the MINIMUM age for their gender
WITH min_age AS (
    SELECT "gender", MIN("age") AS "min_age"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
    GROUP BY "gender"
)
SELECT u."id", u."gender", u."age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS u
JOIN min_age m
  ON u."gender" = m."gender"
 AND u."age"    = m."min_age"
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: count how many users have the MINIMUM age per gender
WITH min_age AS (
    SELECT "gender", MIN("age") AS "min_age"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
    GROUP BY "gender"
)
SELECT u."gender",
       m."min_age",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_users_at_min_age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS u
JOIN min_age m
  ON u."gender" = m."gender"
 AND u."age"    = m."min_age"
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY u."gender", m."min_age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: count how many users have the MAXIMUM age per gender
WITH max_age AS (
    SELECT "gender", MAX("age") AS "max_age"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
    GROUP BY "gender"
)
SELECT u."gender",
       x."max_age",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_users_at_max_age"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS u
JOIN max_age x
  ON u."gender" = x."gender"
 AND u."age"    = x."max_age"
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY u."gender", x."max_age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: union of minimum‑age counts and maximum‑age counts for quick comparison
WITH min_age AS (
    SELECT "gender", MIN("age") AS "edge_age", 'MIN' AS "edge_type"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
    GROUP BY "gender"
), max_age AS (
    SELECT "gender", MAX("age") AS "edge_age", 'MAX' AS "edge_type"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
    GROUP BY "gender"
), edges AS (
    SELECT * FROM min_age
    UNION ALL
    SELECT * FROM max_age
)
SELECT e."gender",
       e."edge_type",
       e."edge_age",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_users"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS u
JOIN edges e
  ON u."gender" = e."gender"
 AND u."age"    = e."edge_age"
WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
GROUP BY e."gender", e."edge_type", e."edge_age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: single final query that returns, for each gender, 
--                 the minimum age, #users at min age, maximum age, #users at max age
WITH min_age AS (
    SELECT "gender", MIN("age") AS "min_age"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
    GROUP BY "gender"
), max_age AS (
    SELECT "gender", MAX("age") AS "max_age"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS
    WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
    GROUP BY "gender"
), min_cnt AS (
    SELECT u."gender", COUNT(*) AS "min_age_user_cnt"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS u
    JOIN min_age m
      ON u."gender" = m."gender" AND u."age" = m."min_age"
    WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
    GROUP BY u."gender"
), max_cnt AS (
    SELECT u."gender", COUNT(*) AS "max_age_user_cnt"
    FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.USERS u
    JOIN max_age x
      ON u."gender" = x."gender" AND u."age" = x."max_age"
    WHERE u."created_at" BETWEEN 1546300800000000 AND 1651363199000000
    GROUP BY u."gender"
)
SELECT m."gender",
       m."min_age",
       mc."min_age_user_cnt",
       x."max_age",
       xc."max_age_user_cnt"
FROM min_age m
JOIN max_age x  ON m."gender" = x."gender"
JOIN min_cnt mc ON m."gender" = mc."gender"
JOIN max_cnt xc ON m."gender" = xc."gender"
LIMIT 20;
```

Running the last statement (#10) will yield exactly what the business question is asking for: for males and females, the youngest age, how many users share that age, the oldest age, and how many users share that age, bounded by signup dates from 2019‑01‑01 to 2022‑04‑30.
